.TH CWE-416 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-416 \- Use After Free
.SH RANK
2025 CWE Top 25 rank: \fB#7\fR (2024 rank: 8).
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: Memory Safety.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Memory is referenced after being freed. The freed block may be reallocated for another purpose, so the dangling pointer aliases unrelated data; results range from crashes to information disclosure to attacker\-controlled execution. A C/C++ manual\-memory weakness.
.SH MITIGATION
Null out pointers after free, establish clear ownership, and avoid multiple aliases to freed memory. Use AddressSanitizer/Valgrind; in C++ use smart pointers; consider Rust where its ownership model prevents the class.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB96\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2010\-0249
Microsoft Internet Explorer, added 2026\-05\-20.
.PP
Microsoft Internet Explorer Use\-After\-Free Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Microsoft Internet Explorer contains an use\-after\-free vulnerability that could allow remote attackers to execute arbitrary code by accessing a pointer associated with a deleted object. The impacted product could be end\-of\-life (EoL) and/or end\-of\-service (EoS). Users should discontinue product utilization.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, or discontinue use.
 Due 2026\-06\-03.
.PP
